  "query": "I've been living on instant coffee and I'm finally ready to make the real thing at home, but the coffee aisle is intimidating: single-origin bags that cost triple the supermarket blend, dark roasts that promise 'bold caffeine kick', whole-bean bags I'd need to figure out how to deal with, and one little stovetop espresso pot that claims cafe-quality without a machine. Which of the things people repeat about coffee are actually true, like whether dark roast really has more caffeine or beans really go stale in weeks? And what would you honestly start a beginner on from what's out there, without me buying gear I'll abandon by spring?",
